    "https://www.keystone.edu/career-services/": {
      "title": "Career Development Center",
      "description": "Career Development - Keystone College 1-800-824-2764 admissions@keystone.edu Calendar Directory QUICK LINKS Bookstore Buy Keystone Gear Resident Dining Current Students Faculty & Staff Library News Visiting Give Now How to Apply About Keystone Accreditations and Authorizations Campus & La Plume Community College Publications and Media History of Keystone Mission, Vision, Strategic Plan Office of the President Student Consumer Information Your Community Partner Departments and Office Hours Admissions Visit Why Choose Keystone? Undergraduate International Students Tuition and Aid Accepted Students Parents Veteran and Military Students Academics Majors, Minors Online Programs Graduate Programs Schools and Programs Career Development Student Success Center Meet Our Faculty Registrar Study Abroad Dual Enrollment/High School Programs Apprenticeship Programs Honors Program Undergraduate Research Continuing Education Online Degree Programs Professional Development Programs (Online) Customized Workforce Training Credit Certificates and Workforce Education Self-Paced Courses and Certificates Personal Enrichment Certificates and Credentials for Educators Community and Recreation Programs KCEEI – Keystone College Environmental Education Institute KC3D Campus Life Activities and Events for Students Campus Resources for Support and Success Dining Belong at Keystone Title IX Policy and Procedures Keystone KeyKard Living on Campus Visiting Campus Alumni Alumni Events, Reunions and Visits Alumni Benefits Our Alumni Get Involved Alumni Oral History Project Giving How to Give Donor Recognition Impact of Giving Naming Opportunities Athletics Select Page APPLY NOW + Career Development Center at Keystone College Whether you’re choosing a major, exploring careers or preparing for internships, we can help you take the next step. Book an appointment Home » Career Development Career Development Ted Williamson Director of Career Development 570-945-8988 ted.williamson@keystone.edu Location: 2nd Floor Hibbard Campus Center Book Appointment Prepare for the career of your dreams. Get the most out of your education and utilize our career services and programs early in your college career, and continue to participate in the Stairs to Success and career development process throughout your time at Keystone. Career Development will work with you to meet all of the requirements of the Keystone Promise and Stairs to Success and help you reach your career or graduate school goals. If you need help with your resume, career documents or grad school applications, email us at careers@keystone.edu . What can we help you with? Need your resume, grad school or career documents reviewed? Email careers@keystone.edu. Choosing a Major Internships Job Preparation Career Exploration Grad School  Faculty Resources We support faculty in their classrooms and help them support students in their career preparation.  Alumni Resources We help alumni clarify career goals or obtain employment and/or admission into a graduate program  Employer Resources We build relationships with the local community and can help you find the right candidate. More Resources For STUDENT Success In addition to the Career Development Center, Keystone offers a variety of resources to help you succeed during your time at Keystone. Reach out to any of us for help, or visit the resources below. Student Success Center Comprehensive support  that caters to the unique needs of each student. Curriculum Guides Recommended semester-by-semester schedule of courses and milestones required for your degree. Tutoring Tutors may be available to meet face-to-face, chat, email, phone, Zoom, Facetime, Skype, etc. Writing Center The Writing Center helps students in all disciplines become more effective writers. We offer just for you “The Keystone College Promise.” A pledge to every Keystone College student that within six months of graduating from Keystone you will have received at least one job offer or been accepted into a transfer or graduate program. Requirements for the Promise Real World Experience You can explore career options through experiential learning and internships within your field of study. Learn about internships. Keeping the Keystone Promise Our pledge that within six months of graduating from Keystone College you will have received at least one job offer or been accepted into a transfer or graduate program. Founded in 1868 and accredited by the Middle States Commission on Higher Education. Maps and Directions. Office Hours: Monday-Friday 8:30 a.m. – 4:30 p.m. One College Green P.O. Box 50 La Plume, PA 18440-0200 1-800-824-2764 or 570-945-8000 Apply Visit Campus Need help? Bookstore Buy Keystone Gear Careers at Keystone College Current Students & Staff Departments and Office Hours Library Student Consumer Information Web Content Policy Web Accessibility Statement Web Disclaimer and Privacy Statement"
    },
    "https://www.keystone.edu/academics/meet-our-faculty/": {
      "title": "Meet Our Faculty",
      "description": "Meet Our Faculty - Keystone College 1-800-824-2764 admissions@keystone.edu Calendar Directory QUICK LINKS Bookstore Buy Keystone Gear Resident Dining Current Students Faculty & Staff Library News Visiting Give Now How to Apply About Keystone Accreditations and Authorizations Campus & La Plume Community College Publications and Media History of Keystone Mission, Vision, Strategic Plan Office of the President Student Consumer Information Your Community Partner Departments and Office Hours Admissions Visit Why Choose Keystone? Undergraduate International Students Tuition and Aid Accepted Students Parents Veteran and Military Students Academics Majors, Minors Online Programs Graduate Programs Schools and Programs Career Development Student Success Center Meet Our Faculty Registrar Study Abroad Dual Enrollment/High School Programs Apprenticeship Programs Honors Program Undergraduate Research Continuing Education Online Degree Programs Professional Development Programs (Online) Customized Workforce Training Credit Certificates and Workforce Education Self-Paced Courses and Certificates Personal Enrichment Certificates and Credentials for Educators Community and Recreation Programs KCEEI – Keystone College Environmental Education Institute KC3D Campus Life Activities and Events for Students Campus Resources for Support and Success Dining Belong at Keystone Title IX Policy and Procedures Keystone KeyKard Living on Campus Visiting Campus Alumni Alumni Events, Reunions and Visits Alumni Benefits Our Alumni Get Involved Alumni Oral History Project Giving How to Give Donor Recognition Impact of Giving Naming Opportunities Athletics Select Page APPLY NOW + Home » Academics » Meet Our Faculty Meet Our Faculty What Makes Keystone College’s Faculty So Special? At Keystone you’ll be surrounded by teachers and mentors who are leading experts in their chosen fields. They bring real-world experience and creativity to the classroom to create a dynamic learning environment. Our professors are committed to students and encourage and inspire them to think globally and critically.  Expertise and Research Members of our faculty are experts in their respective fields. Many have come to Keystone after achieving success and completing groundbreaking research in their own respective professions and fields of study.  Faculty Mentors Keystone College students and faculty often work together to undertake significant research projects at the undergraduate and graduate level. This opportunity fosters one-on-one working relationships and develops connections that last a lifetime.  Teaching At Keystone, our faculty is dedicated to teaching our students and helping them succeed.  Individual Attention Our class sizes are small and our faculty is dedicated to giving students the individual attention they expect and deserve. Faculty News All-College Honors Convocation 2026 recognizes achievements April 30, 2026 Keystone College Adjunct Professor Receives Approval to Advance Research on CFO Leadership & Digital Transformation March 18, 2026 Dr. Joe Iacovazzi Engages Young Readers for Read Across America Week March 6, 2026 No results found. More faculty news »  102 Faculty, including full time, part time and visiting.  10:1 Student to faculty ratio. Faculty Profiles Directory Karen Arcangelo, PhD, NCSP Professor of Education Deborah Doyle Belknap, JD, PhD Associate Professor of Criminal Justice and Psychology Jeffrey M. Brauer Professor of Political Science and Faculty Coordinator of First Year Seminar William Chase II, PsyD Associate Professor of Psychology and Chair of Social and Behavioral Sciences Department Kasey Chermak Program Director for Computer Science and Information Technology Robert D. Cook, PhD, PG Professor of Physical Science Patricia Davis, PhD Professor of Accounting Anthony DelRegno Assistant Professor of Communications and Digital Media Kassandra Ford, M.Acc Program Director for Business, Management & Technology hybrid programs Steven R. Howell, PhD Professor of Psychology Joseph Iacovazzi, PhD Chair of Biological and Physical Sciences and Mathematics Jan Kaskey Professor of Education Brenda Lidy Chair of Business, Management, and Technology Laura Little, DBA Program Director of MBA and SLM Caroline Millen, PhD Assistant Professor of Education Patricia Bederman Miller, PhD Professor of Mathematics John B. Minora Instructor of Chemistry Ryan Novitsky Program Director for eSport and Gaming Managment Youyu Phillips, PhD Professor of Mathematics Jeanie Prall Chair of the Education Department Patrick M. Ratchford, PhD Assistant Professor of Mathematics Gina Rice Instructor of Art Kerry Roe, PhD Associate Professor of History Ward Roe Professor of Art James van Sandwyk, Ph.D. Assistant Professor of Biology Ronda Schiavone, MBA Program Director of Business and Hospitality Business Management Brandon Smith Instructor of Art Sherry S. Strain, PhD Professor of Communications Linda Tucker, PhD Assistant Professor of Botany Rachel Urbanowicz Chair of Communications, Art, and Humanities Department Kevin Vinson Associate Professor and Program Director of Accounting, B.S., and Financial Planning, B.S. Sara White Assistant Professor of English and Journalism Stacey Wyland Associate Professor of Criminal Justice No results found. What Our Students Say “Everyone here is nice and it’s like a close-knit family. The professors are great. They want me to succeed.” Rolando Rodriguez | Major: Pre-Physical Therapy “The professors and teachers really helped me. If you show you want to learn, they go out of their way to assist you.” Felix Baez | Major: Accounting “My education at Keystone helped make my dreams possible. Faculty members like Terry Wise and Janet DeAndrea really helped put me on the right career path and made sure I stayed there.” Scott Gower '06 | Athletic Director at Keystone College Founded in 1868 and accredited by the Middle States Commission on Higher Education. Maps and Directions. Office Hours: Monday-Friday 8:30 a.m. – 4:30 p.m. One College Green P.O. Box 50 La Plume, PA 18440-0200 1-800-824-2764 or 570-945-8000 Apply Visit Campus Need help? Bookstore Buy Keystone Gear Careers at Keystone College Current Students & Staff Departments and Office Hours Library Student Consumer Information Web Content Policy Web Accessibility Statement Web Disclaimer and Privacy Statement"
    },
    "https://www.keystone.edu/2026/05/18/adjunct-faculty-law/": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty – Law",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty – Law - Keystone College 1-800-824-2764 admissions@keystone.edu Calendar Directory QUICK LINKS Bookstore Buy Keystone Gear Resident Dining Current Students Faculty & Staff Library News Visiting Give Now How to Apply About Keystone Accreditations and Authorizations Campus & La Plume Community College Publications and Media History of Keystone Mission, Vision, Strategic Plan Office of the President Student Consumer Information Your Community Partner Departments and Office Hours Admissions Visit Why Choose Keystone? Undergraduate International Students Tuition and Aid Accepted Students Parents Veteran and Military Students Academics Majors, Minors Online Programs Graduate Programs Schools and Programs Career Development Student Success Center Meet Our Faculty Registrar Study Abroad Dual Enrollment/High School Programs Apprenticeship Programs Honors Program Undergraduate Research Continuing Education Online Degree Programs Professional Development Programs (Online) Customized Workforce Training Credit Certificates and Workforce Education Self-Paced Courses and Certificates Personal Enrichment Certificates and Credentials for Educators Community and Recreation Programs KCEEI – Keystone College Environmental Education Institute KC3D Campus Life Activities and Events for Students Campus Resources for Support and Success Dining Belong at Keystone Title IX Policy and Procedures Keystone KeyKard Living on Campus Visiting Campus Alumni Alumni Events, Reunions and Visits Alumni Benefits Our Alumni Get Involved Alumni Oral History Project Giving How to Give Donor Recognition Impact of Giving Naming Opportunities Athletics Select Page APPLY NOW + Home » Uncategorized » Adjunct Faculty – Law Adjunct Faculty – Law May 18, 2026 | Job Posting - Faculty , Uncategorized Business, Management, and Technology Division Adjunct Faculty – Law (Part-Time) The Adjunct Law Faculty member teaches undergraduate or graduate-level law courses on a part-time, contractual basis. This role brings practical legal experience into the classroom while supporting student learning and engagement. Responsibilities: Teach assigned law course(s) and deliver engaging lectures Develop and follow course syllabus and learning outcomes Create and grade assignments, exams, and assessments Provide timely feedback and submit final grades Hold limited office hours to support and advise students Stay current in legal practice and incorporate real-world applications Qualifications: J.D. (or equivalent law degree); bar admission preferred Professional legal experience in relevant field Prior teaching experience preferred Strong communication and organizational skills Additional Information: Part-time, per-course appointment (semester-based) Course offering: morning, afternoon, or evening. Course Delivery: Face-2-Face. TO APPLY: Please send resume, cover letter, and names, addresses & phone numbers of three professional references to:  Human Resources * Keystone College * One College Green * La Plume, PA 18440-1099 * email:  humanresources@keystone.edu News by Category Academic News Alumni News Campus News Event News Faculty/Staff Featured News In the News Student News Veteran News News Archives 2023 2022 2021 2020 2019 2018 Founded in 1868 and accredited by the Middle States Commission on Higher Education. Maps and Directions. Office Hours: Monday-Friday 8:30 a.m. – 4:30 p.m. One College Green P.O. Box 50 La Plume, PA 18440-0200 1-800-824-2764 or 570-945-8000 Apply Visit Campus Need help? Bookstore Buy Keystone Gear Careers at Keystone College Current Students & Staff Departments and Office Hours Library Student Consumer Information Web Content Policy Web Accessibility Statement Web Disclaimer and Privacy Statement"
